    "latest_update": "R-136 proves the conditional-centring contraction and the exact random-operator defect for admissible operators whose displayed products and conditional expectations are square-integrable, identifies the literal deterministic-target-heat R-088 post-heat atom as future-residual zero, formally rejects post-heat mean-only variance recovery, and recovers the exact R-125 owner through common-heat future replicas and a raw per-replica sequential telescope. It reuses the forward Doob/OU coordinate without reclaiming R-102 and records the load-bearing R-079 feedback correction. The abstract graph-compression observation weakens a route assumption but supplies no production estimate. The raw projected atom bound, once-owned shell ledger, positive headroom, production low and matching data, strict gap, absolute anchor, and both A13 gates remain open.",
    "success_condition": "Prove A13-CLASSII-COMMON-HEAT-REPLICA-RAW-CURRENT-SEQUENTIAL-ONE-USE-BOUND. Construct the complete raw reveal derivative before future heat for every recombined owner, including the complete low endpoint, all same-root visits, exhaustive output clusters, both R-079 feedback channels, all six signed Pauli--Fierz rows, trace, rational and 2680/729 Cartan companions, and common heat. Prove 2 int_0^infinity e^(-2t) E||Pi_m P_t^(r) T_hat_(r,k)||_HS^2 dt <= 2^(-2s(m-k)) q_k with s=2/3, deterministic q_k>=0, and sum_k q_k<=Q, without freezing later feedback, using the rejected extracted-Z6 envelope, or introducing owner/reveal/visit/cluster multiplicity. Then apply the R-135 nonorthogonal gamma=7/12 sum, certify positive near/balanced headroom at one finite collar, prove the complete low and matching data, strict gap, and absolute anchor, apply R-129 once, and only then continue through R-093 toward OVERLAP_src and Nelson. Removals, interacting-measure construction, and Sector A remain open."
